 that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-denominator-sandwich"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-denominator-sandwich"],"id":"long.lem-denominator-sandwich","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.55 (The odd denominator survives dyadic subtraction)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.55, p. 59, label lem:denominator-sandwich","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $r/D$ be a reduced fraction with $D>0$ odd, let $p\\in\\mathbb Z$, and let $c\\ge0$ be an integer. The reduced denominator of $p/2^c-r/D$ is divisible by $D$ and divides $2^cD$. Indeed, its unreduced numerator $pD-2^cr$ is coprime to $D$, since $\\gcd(r,D)=\\gcd(2^c,D)=1$. Reduction can therefore remove only powers of $2$ from the displayed denominator. No property of Mersenne weights is used.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-denominator-sandwich","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-denominator-sandwich","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-sandwich%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidualIntNumerator_coprime_oddDenominator%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-denominator-sandwich%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidualIntNumerator_coprime_oddDenominator%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidualIntNumerator_coprime_oddDenominator"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-denominator-sandwich","id":